405	\begin{example}[Conditional extraction given a global polynomial-pair witness]
406		\label{lem:qld-unitary-given-global-pair}
407		\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_extractionWitness_ofGlobalPairWitness}
408		\uses{lem:qld-4-7, def:v-swap-unitary, def:expanded-state,
409			lem:projective-strategy-setup, def:generalized-pauli, def:EPR,
410			def:povm-distance}
411		This formalization-only auxiliary is not a named statement of the paper. It is
412		the conditional, given-witness form
413		of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary}: the projective global polynomial-pair measurement
414		$\{\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\}$ of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, together with the two
415		point-consistency estimates that lemma asserts at a parameter $\delta_G \geq 0$,
416		is assumed as data rather than obtained from that lemma. There is a universal
417		constant $C_{\mathrm{ext}} \geq 1$ such that the following holds for every
418		admissible $(q,m,d)$, every $0 \leq \eps \leq 1$, every projective strategy
419		setup at error $\eps$ (Lemma~\ref{lem:projective-strategy-setup}), every
420		$\delta_G \geq 0$, and every assumed measurement as above. The swap unitaries
421		$V_{\mathrm{A}}$ and $V_{\mathrm{B}}$ built from that measurement by
422		Definition~\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} are two-sided unitaries, and there is a
423		normalized state $\ket{\mathrm{aux}}$ on registers
424		$\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$ for which items 1 and 2 of
425		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} hold at the scale $\delta_{\mathrm{qld}}$ of that
426		lemma, computed from $\eps$ and the assumed $\delta_G$.
427		The assumed measurement is proof debt rather than a faithful boundary
428		hypothesis: Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} obtains it from
429		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7} before constructing the swap unitaries. Eliminating
430		the assumption requires carrying out that construction first; this missing
431		composition is recorded in \cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.
432		The corresponding proof obligation repeats the argument of
433		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} above, using the assumed
434		measurement in place of the appeal to Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7}.
435	\end{example}
